 ## Background
-SubSplat was proposed by Jiun Lee et al. in 2024 [S1]. It addresses the limitations of pixel-aligned Gaussian methods that are constrained by fixed grids or suffer from high computational costs at high resolutions. It uses the same input structure as MVSplat and incorporates a deformable-attention operator following the formulation used in GaussianFormer and PixelGaussian [S1]. It is used for novel-view synthesis in computer vision, specifically for sparse-view reconstruction [S1].
